The C version of Life on sparse tiles (benchmarks/life/life-sparse.c),
which compare-sparse.sh runs against life-sparse.m, on the machine's GPU:
its population, checksum and active tiles are life-sparse.m's, and the
dense programs' for the same world (life-sparse.test), the default world
too.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: clang -O2 -fopenmp --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/../../benchmarks/life/life-sparse.c -o %t
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY LIFE_WORLD=256 LIFE_TILE=16 LIFE_SOUP=64 LIFE_STEPS=50 timeout -k 1 60 %t | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=A
A: Game of Life, C, sparse tiles
A-NEXT: World: 256 x 256 cells, tiles of 16 x 16, 256 in the pool
A-NEXT: Soup: 64 x 64 cells at the centre
A-NEXT: Steps: 50
A-NEXT: Population: 562
A-NEXT: Checksum: 17668223
A-NEXT: Active tiles: 36 at most, 32 at the end
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY LIFE_WORLD=200 LIFE_TILE=8 LIFE_SOUP=37 LIFE_STEPS=120 timeout -k 1 60 %t | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ODD
ODD: Population: 157
ODD-NEXT: Checksum: 2963654
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY LIFE_WORLD=256 LIFE_TILE=8 LIFE_SOUP=256 LIFE_STEPS=100 timeout -k 1 60 %t | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WHOLE
WHOLE: Population: 4947
WHOLE-NEXT: Checksum: 158368224
WHOLE-NEXT: Active tiles: 1024 at most, 856 at the end
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY timeout -k 1 60 %t | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DEFAULT
DEFAULT: World: 8192 x 8192 cells, tiles of 64 x 64, 8192 in the pool
DEFAULT: Population: 3719
DEFAULT-NEXT: Checksum: 124925383998
DEFAULT-NEXT: Active tiles: 45 at most, 43 at the end
RUN: %libomp-env OMP_TARGET_OFFLOAD=MANDATORY LIFE_WORLD=256 LIFE_TILE=8 LIFE_SOUP=256 LIFE_STEPS=10 LIFE_CAPACITY=100 not %t | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=FULL
FULL: The pool ran out of tiles: raise LIFE_CAPACITY.
